{
 "about": "Where a plate has to be for each kind of work, and how it gets there (issue #63). 'move-on': the plate is placed onto or into the module or device, so reaching it is a move. 'in-place': the module acts on a plate that stays where it is (a magnet that rises under the plate). 'pipetting' says whether the pipettes can reach a plate in that position. Entries without a source take the default, which is marked as such. Move times are planning estimates.",
 "default": {
  "mode": "move-on",
  "pipetting": true,
  "basis": "default: the plate is placed onto the module (no source states otherwise)"
 },
 "devices": {
  "mode": "move-on",
  "pipetting": false,
  "basis": "a connected device off the deck is its own position, reached by an arm or a person"
 },
